dsv41 patch 0061 (20.10.2026): FP8 sliding window + NVFP4 compressed KV, two FlashInfer calls merged by their LSE. In the
image, off: rejected (KV-KLD and decode speed, see below). Base: the v11 files (0060).
Why: vLLM's own nvfp4_ds_mla format (SM100 only) keeps the fp8_ds_mla record for the sliding window and stores only the
compressed KV as NVFP4 (DeepInfer: FP4 for the main KV), and 0059 lost most in the first positions. FlashInfer's SM120
kernel reads its window and compressed pools in one format only.
How: VLLM_DSV41_KV_NVFP4=2: the window pages stay FP8 (576 B alignment), compressed and indexer pages are NVFP4 / FP8 at
512 B, the block stride aligned to lcm(576, 512) = 4,608 B. split_sparse_mla calls FlashInfer's
_trtllm_batch_decode_sparse_mla_sm120 twice with return_lse (window FP8, compressed NVFP4, both without the attention
sink) and merges in a Triton kernel: the LSE is base 2 (FlashInfer's docstring says natural log; with base e the merge
is 9-16 % off in our unit test), the sink enters the merge's denominator, an empty compressed segment (LSE < -1e29) gets
weight 0. Decode and prefill; our Triton verify off. GPU unit test: FP8 decode split + merge = one call within 0.25-0.29 %
(relative L2); NVFP4 and FP8 prefill 1.8-4 % apart, because the kernel quantizes P for the P*V MMA relative to each call's
own maximum (decode_dsv4_nvfp4_kernel.cuh), so two calls round differently from one.
Measured (21.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v12 with 0060, one window against FP8 with 0057): KV pool 1,837,489 tokens
(0060 alone: 1,531,258), 1,522 B per token live, needles at 250K 6/6, cost per verify round -0.7 % (geometric mean), but
tok/s -2.8 %: fewer drafts accepted (tokens per round -3.9 %, JSON at T=0 -22.5 %); KV-KLD KL 0.0146 / top-1 96.56 %
against FP8 records (run-to-run floor of the measurement KL ~0.008 / top-1 ~97.5 %), first 127 positions KL 0.106
prose / 0.044 code. Not adopted.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_KV_NVFP4=2 (default 0 = off; 1 = 0059).
